    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d155">

                <pb facs="0196" n="182" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg182"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">839.415/146: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Dominican Republic</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Warren</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ciudad Trujillo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-02-17T11:00:00-05:00">February 17,
                            1944—11 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 3:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>101. President Trujillo has informed me that he has drafted a reply to President
                    Lescot’s letter of February 12 and he wanted me to see it first. I suggested
                    that he might care to withhold any letter for the time being in view of the
                    possibility that President Lescot may reconsider his position. He said he wished
                    the Department to be informed he still considered invitation open
                    notwithstanding President Lescot’s letter and he is prepared to meet the latter
                    any day during the Centennial celebration with the exception of February 22 when
                    Andrews <pb facs="0197" n="183" xml:id="pg183"/> Field will be dedicated and
                    February 27 when the schedule of events requiring his presence is so heavy as to
                    preclude; his leaving the capital. In this connection please refer to my
                    telegram number 91 of February 14, 7 p.m. and Ambassador White’s telegram of
                    February 16, 3 p.m.<anchor n="38" xml:id="d155-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Repeated to Port-au-Prince.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Warren</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d155-f1" n="38" xml:id="d155-f1-content">
                <p>Latter not found in Department files. Ambassador Warren may be referring to
                    Ambassador White’s telegram 40, February 15, 5 p.m., <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
